@page "/"

<PageTitle>Offline CRUD</PageTitle>

<section class="hero mb-5">
    <p class="text-uppercase small fw-semibold mb-2 opacity-75">Blazor WebAssembly · Learning project</p>
    <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-3">A CRUD app that keeps working when the network doesn't</h1>
    <p class="lead mb-4">
        A product catalogue that runs entirely in your browser. Edits are saved locally first, queued in an outbox,
        and synced to the API whenever a connection is available.
    </p>
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a href="products" class="btn btn-light btn-lg">
            <i class="bi bi-box-seam me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>Browse products
        </a>
        <a href="about" class="btn btn-outline-light btn-lg">How it works</a>
    </div>
</section>

<h2 class="h4 mb-3">What this project demonstrates</h2>
<div class="row g-4 mb-5">
    <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <span class="feature-icon mb-3"><i class="bi bi-browser-chrome" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
                <h3 class="h6">.NET in the browser</h3>
                <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                    The whole app, including its C# business logic, is downloaded and runs on WebAssembly.
                    There's no server connection like Blazor Server's to lean on.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <span class="feature-icon mb-3"><i class="bi bi-database" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
                <h3 class="h6">Local-first storage</h3>
                <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                    IndexedDB holds the data the UI shows, so lists and edits work without a connection.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <span class="feature-icon mb-3"><i class="bi bi-arrow-repeat" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
                <h3 class="h6">Outbox and sync</h3>
                <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                    Each change is recorded in an outbox and replayed in order, with retries and backoff,
                    once the app is back online.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-3">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <span class="feature-icon mb-3"><i class="bi bi-layers" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
                <h3 class="h6">Clean Architecture</h3>
                <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                    Domain and use cases know nothing about the browser. IndexedDB, HTTP and JS interop sit at the edges.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <div class="card-body d-flex flex-column flex-md-row gap-3 align-items-md-center">
        <i class="bi bi-cone-striped fs-2 text-warning" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <div class="flex-grow-1">
            <h2 class="h6 mb-1">Built in phases</h2>
            <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">
                This build is Phase 4: everything works offline. Flip "Simulate offline" in the menu bar (or use
                DevTools → Network → Offline), make some changes, and watch them queue on the Sync page and drain when
                you're back online.
            </p>
        </div>
        <a href="about#roadmap" class="btn btn-outline-primary text-nowrap">See the roadmap</a>
    </div>
</div>
